    "description": "<p>We give an explicit irreducible matrix N of order six with unit-disk numerical range and a 2 by 2 matrix polynomial P satisfying max over the unit disk of ||P(z)|| = 1 and ||P[N]|| = 2. Every compression by constant complex unit coefficient vectors u and v nevertheless satisfies ||(v* P u)(N)|| &lt;= sqrt(849)/16 &lt; 2. The matrix is twice a member of the classical Li-Spitkovsky-Shukla family. A simple top singular pair provides a finite certificate of equality and of the obstruction to scalar coefficient compression. All assertions follow from explicit matrix calculations.</p>",
    "references": [
      {
        "reference": "P. Åhag, R. Czyż, and J. Virtanen, The Complete Crouzeix Conjecture in Dimension Three and the Clouâtre–Ostermann–Ransford conjecture, arXiv:2608.27346v4, 2026."
      },
      {
        "reference": "M. Crouzeix, Bounds for analytical functions of matrices, Integral Equations Operator Theory 48 (2004), 461–477. doi:10.1007/s00020-002-1188-6."
      },
      {
        "reference": "M. Crouzeix, Numerical range and functional calculus in Hilbert space, J. Funct. Anal. 244 (2007), 668–690. doi:10.1016/j.jfa.2006.10.013."
      },
      {
        "reference": "M. Crouzeix and C. Palencia, The numerical range is a (1 + sqrt(2))-spectral set, SIAM J. Matrix Anal. Appl. 38 (2017), 649–655. doi:10.1137/17M1116672."
      },
      {
        "reference": "S. Jin, The numerical range is a 2-spectral set, Preprints.org, manuscript 202607.1919, version 4, 2026. doi:10.20944/preprints202607.1919.v4."
      },
      {
        "reference": "E. Lorist and F. L. Schwenninger, A solution to Crouzeix's conjecture, arXiv:2608.03841v2, 2026."
      },
      {
        "reference": "M. Kang, Scalar extremizers for complete Crouzeix equality in dimension four, preprint, 2026. doi:10.5281/zenodo.23332163."
      },
